  "live_records": {
    "q-213247": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213247",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Consider the following relation defined on the set $A=\\{-1,2,6,9\\}.$ \n\n$$\nR=\\{(-1,-1),(2,2),(2,6),(6,6)\\}\n$$\n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:\n\nSince \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}, \n\nthe relation is \n{{field-3}}.",
      "worked_solution": "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nIn our case, the relation is defined on $\\{-1,2,6,9\\},$ and we have\n\n$$\n(-1,-1)\\in R,\\,(2,2)\\in R,\\,(6,6)\\in R,\\,(9,9)\\notin R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude the following:\n\n$\\,$ Since $(9,9)\\notin R$ $\\text{and }(6,6)\\in R,$ the relation is $\\text{neither reflexive nor irreflexive}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
